  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Section 2 Model, p.5",
  "quote": "Sortition, the random selection of political representatives",
  "note": "The paper studies sortition selection algorithms. These randomly choose a quota-satisfying panel from a pool of volunteers based on the features the volunteers report. The inputs are demographic features, not votes, ballots or preferences over alternatives, and no collective decision is reached by voting. It is closer to constrained random selection or fair allocation of selection probability than to a voting procedure. Coding stopped per C0."
